// 🔷 ARCHITECTURAL ROLE
//
// Group 5 is the **highest authority control plane layer**.
//
// It governs:
//
//   ✔ shard placement authority
//   ✔ CPU + NUMA binding enforcement
//   ✔ runtime lifecycle (start / stop / freeze)
//   ✔ structural immutability guarantees
//
// It depends on:
//
//   Group 3 → topology + shard ownership source of truth
//   Group 4 → state evolution + cryptographic execution history
//
// It does NOT:
//   ✘ execute workloads
//   ✘ compute state transitions
